'उत्तर प्रदेशमा सहायता प्राप्त माध्यमिक विद्यालयहरूमा १,४७५ प्रधानाचार्य र १,१७२ प्रधानाध्यापक पद खुलेका छन्, लिखित परीक्षा ७ जनवरी २०२७ मा हुनेछ।',
$$<p>The Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (UPESSC), Prayagraj, has opened applications for 2,647 school leadership posts in the state's aided non-government secondary schools. The recruitment covers two advertisements: 1,475 Principal (Pradhanacharya) posts under advertisement 08/2026 and 1,172 Headmaster (Pradhanadhyapak) posts under advertisement 09/2026. Online applications opened on 23 October 2026 and close on 22 November 2026, with the written examination scheduled for 7 January 2027.</p>
<p>This is a rare opening at this scale. Principal and Headmaster posts are the top of a teaching career, they open far less often than classroom teacher vacancies, and these 2,647 posts are spread across boys' and girls' institutions throughout Uttar Pradesh. Candidates should note one unusual condition up front: according to the commission's coverage, all 2,647 vacancies are unreserved, and no age relaxation applies to any category.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Conducting body</th><td>Uttar Pradesh Education Service Selection Commission (UPESSC), Prayagraj</td></tr>
<tr><th>Posts</th><td>2,647 — Principal 1,475 (Advt 08/2026), Headmaster 1,172 (Advt 09/2026)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Schools</th><td>Aided non-government secondary schools, Uttar Pradesh</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>23 October to 22 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Correction window</th><td>Until 25 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Written exam</th><td>7 January 2027</td></tr>
<tr><th>Exam pattern</th><td>120 objective questions, 360 marks (+3 / -1), plus 40-mark interview</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age</th><td>30 to 62 years as on 1 July 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Official portal</th><td><a href="https://upessc.up.gov.in">upessc.up.gov.in</a></td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p>For teachers, these are destination posts. A Principal or Headmaster runs the whole institution, and the pay reflects that: Principal posts sit at Pay Level-12, from Rs 78,800 to Rs 2,09,200 per month, while Headmaster posts carry Rs 56,100 to Rs 1,77,500. The selection also reflects the seniority of the role. Unlike a classroom teacher recruitment, this one adds a 40-mark interview on top of the written examination, so subject knowledge alone is not enough; candidates will also be judged on leadership and administrative judgement.</p>
<p>The scale matters too. UPESSC released both notifications on the same day, 23 October, which means experienced teachers can assess both posts together and choose the one that fits their service record. The catch is the eligibility bar: this is not an entry-level drive. It is designed for teachers who have already spent years in classrooms, and the experience condition will filter out most applicants before the examination even begins.</p>
<h2>Key details</h2>
<p>The Principal vacancies split into 1,318 posts in boys' inter colleges and 157 in girls' inter colleges. The Headmaster vacancies split into 1,037 in boys' schools and 135 in girls' schools. The gender rules matter here: male candidates cannot be appointed as Principal in a girls' institution, and for Headmaster posts, male candidates may apply only for boys' schools while female candidates may apply for either category but must select only one. Choosing the wrong category is an unforced error, so check the school-wise requisition list in the notification before applying.</p>
<p>On eligibility, Principal applicants need post-graduation with 50 percent marks plus a B.Ed from an NCTE-recognised institution, together with four years of teaching experience as a Lecturer or Assistant Teacher in Classes 9 to 12, or four years of experience as a High School Headmaster. Headmaster applicants need post-graduation with 50 percent marks, B.Ed or BPEd, and the same four-year teaching or headship experience. The age window is 30 to 62 years as on 1 July 2026. The application fee is Rs 2,000 for Principal posts and Rs 1,500 for Headmaster posts, for all categories, paid online. The written examination carries negative marking: each correct answer earns 3 marks and each wrong or multiple answer loses 1 mark, so blind guessing will cost marks.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>Start at <a href="https://upessc.up.gov.in">upessc.up.gov.in</a> and complete the One Time Registration first; applications without OTR are rejected. Then select the correct advertisement, 08/2026 for Principal or 09/2026 for Headmaster, and fill the form in English with your personal, educational and service details. Upload the photograph, signature and documents, including proof of your teaching experience, because the four-year condition is verified from service records. Pay the fee online by 22 November 2026, submit, and save a printout of the confirmation. The correction window runs until 25 November, but the commission states that category, date of birth and gender cannot be changed after final submission, so get those three fields right the first time.</p>
<p>For preparation, the written examination on 7 January 2027 leaves roughly ten weeks from the application deadline. That is enough time to revise the syllabus properly, but not enough to start from zero. Candidates who are serious should begin with the official syllabus and the previous pattern of UPESSC leadership examinations rather than generic teaching-aptitude material.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>UPESSC recruits for aided schools, which are privately managed but government-aided institutions that form a large part of Uttar Pradesh's secondary education system. Their leadership posts have historically been filled slowly, often leaving schools under acting heads for years. A combined notification of this size is therefore a genuine attempt to clear the backlog, and it explains why the commission has paired a written examination with an interview: it wants heads who can run schools, not just pass papers. For the wider region, the drive is also a reminder of how India's state commissions recruit senior educators, a model quite different from Nepal's own teacher service examinations.</p>
<p>One honest takeaway: if you meet the four-year experience bar and the age window, this is a leadership opportunity that may not repeat at this scale soon. If you do not meet the experience condition, no amount of examination preparation will substitute for it.</p>$$,
$$<p>उत्तर प्रदेश शिक्षा सेवा चयन आयोग (UPESSC), प्रयागराजले राज्यका सहायता प्राप्त गैर-सरकारी माध्यमिक विद्यालयहरूमा २,६४७ विद्यालय नेतृत्व पदका लागि आवेदन खुलाएको छ। यस भर्तीमा दुई विज्ञापन छन्: विज्ञापन ०८/२०२६ अन्तर्गत १,४७५ प्रधानाचार्य (प्रधानाचार्य) पद र विज्ञापन ०९/२०२६ अन्तर्गत १,१७२ प्रधानाध्यापक (प्रधानाध्यापक) पद। अनलाइन आवेदन २३ अक्टोबर २०२६ मा खुलेको हो र २२ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा बन्द हुन्छ, लिखित परीक्षा ७ जनवरी २०२७ मा हुनेछ।</p>
<p>यो यस स्तरमा दुर्लभ अवसर हो। प्रधानाचार्य र प्रधानाध्यापक पद शिक्षण करिअरको शिखर हुन्, कक्षा शिक्षकका रिक्तताभन्दा धेरै कम पटक खुल्छन्, र यी २,६४७ पद उत्तर प्रदेशभरका बालक र बालिका विद्यालयहरूमा फैलिएका छन्। एउटा असामान्य शर्त सुरुमै जान्नुहोस्: आयोगको जानकारीअनुसार सबै २,६४७ रिक्तता अनारक्षित छन्, र कुनै पनि वर्गका लागि उमेरमा छुट लागू हुँदैन।</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
